I rebuilt the booking module on a new architecture. Search and pricing results are cached for similar queries, supplier calls run in parallel, and the flow has fewer steps: I removed the booking confirmation modal and the recap page, and compacted the data and the interface so agents decide faster. I also deferred the background calls that block the page. Fetching ancillaries took a good share of the time, yet my research showed fewer than 10% of agents book ancillaries at checkout, so they now load without holding the flow up. I integrated 8 travel suppliers through their SOAP APIs. Then I built NDC booking split and flight exchange for Air France-KLM. In December 2024 Metis became the first technology provider to offer the split.
